    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, quick question. i'm trying to clean up a schema we've been using for a while. we're currently in 2NF but there's a lot of redundant data popping up in some of the tables. can you walk me through the steps to get us to 3NF? specifically how to handle transitive dependencies?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To achieve 3NF, you need to eliminate non-prime attributes that depend on other non-key attributes, which is exactly what transitive dependencies are. Start by identifying all transitive dependencies within your current 2NF candidates, then treat each independent combination of non-key attribute and dependent non-key attribute as a new table. This process effectively splits your existing table into multiple smaller, more normalized tables so that data redundancy is significantly reduced. Finally, update your application code or queries to reference these new tables instead of the old, denormalized structure.",
      "source": "target",
